The keywords are the ones that can come at the cursor, from the stack of the
parser (generated by LRgrep), with the construct they start or continue.

At the start of an expression:

  $ cat >test.ml <<'EOF'
  > let x =
  > EOF
  $ $MERLIN single complete-prefix -position 1:8 -filename test.ml \
  > -kind k -prefix "" < test.ml | jq -r '.value.entries[] | select(.kind == "Keyword") | .name + ": " + .desc'
  function: function <cases>
  let: let [rec] <binding> in <expr>
  fun: fun <params> [':' <type>] -> <expr>
  match: match <expr> with <cases>
  try: try <expr> with <cases>
  if: if <expr> then <expr> [else <expr>]
  while: while <expr> do <expr> done
  for: for <pattern> = <expr> to <expr> do <expr> done
  assert: assert <expr>
  lazy: lazy <expr>
  begin: begin [<expr>] end
  new: new <class>
  object: object <class body> end
  false: false <expr>
  true: true <expr>

In an expression, only the keywords that continue it:

  $ cat >test.ml <<'EOF'
  > let f x = if x t
  > EOF
  $ $MERLIN single complete-prefix -position 1:16 -filename test.ml \
  > -kind k -prefix t < test.ml | jq -r '.value.entries[] | select(.kind == "Keyword") | .name + ": " + .desc'
  then: then <expr> [else <expr>]
  true: true

  $ cat >test.ml <<'EOF'
  > let f x =
  >   match x w
  >   | A -> 1
  > EOF
  $ $MERLIN single complete-prefix -position 2:11 -filename test.ml \
  > -kind k -prefix w < test.ml | jq -r '.value.entries[] | select(.kind == "Keyword") | .name + ": " + .desc'
  with: with <cases>

At the start of a structure item:

  $ cat >test.ml <<'EOF'
  > let x = 1
  > t
  > let y = 2
  > EOF
  $ $MERLIN single complete-prefix -position 2:1 -filename test.ml \
  > -kind k -prefix t < test.ml | jq -r '.value.entries[] | select(.kind == "Keyword") | .name + ": " + .desc'
  true: true
  type: type [nonrec] [<params>] <ident> [= <definition>] [constraint ...]

In a signature:

  $ cat >test.ml <<'EOF'
  > module type S = sig
  >   v
  > end
  > EOF
  $ $MERLIN single complete-prefix -position 2:3 -filename test.ml \
  > -kind k -prefix v < test.ml | jq -r '.value.entries[] | select(.kind == "Keyword") | .name + ": " + .desc'
  val: val <ident> : <type>

The local bindings are kept when completing after a syntax error:

  $ cat >test.ml <<'EOF'
  > let f x = (x + 1
  > let g yyyy = yy
  > EOF
  $ $MERLIN single complete-prefix -position 2:15 -filename test.ml \
  > -prefix yy < test.ml | jq -r '.value.entries[] | .name'
  yyyy
